Section 2. The map (e,v) -> e+v has Jacobian sin(phi-theta) resp. 2 sin(phi-theta)
========================================================================================
PASS  2.1 angle chart: det d(e+v)/d(theta,phi) = sin(phi - theta)   [sin(phi - theta)]
PASS  2.2 (u,w) chart: det = 2 sin(2w) = 2 sin(theta - phi)   [2*sin(2*w)]
PASS  2.3 complex form: det[Je,Jv] = Im(conj(Je) Jv) = sin(phi - theta)   [sin(phi - theta)]
PASS  2.4 the Jacobian vanishes exactly on the diagonal e = +-v (parallel directions)
PASS  2.5 summary: (e,v) -> x+e+v is nonsingular off the null set {e = +-v}

